---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
const updated = 'August 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Terms of use for postheroic.world — a non-commercial storytelling and archive site."
>
  <div class="shell section legal">
    <header class="page-head stack">
      <p class="eyebrow">Last updated {updated}</p>
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose stack">
      <p class="lede">
        This is a non-commercial storytelling and archive site for the novel
        <em>The Very Last Superhero</em>.
      </p>

      <h2>Story, lore and artwork</h2>
      <p>
        All narrative text, lore entries, timeline material and illustrations are &copy; {site.publisher}
        and licensed under
        <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/" rel="license noopener">
          Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International</a
        >.
      </p>
      <p>You are free to share this material, in any medium or format, provided that you:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>give appropriate credit and link back to this site;</li>
        <li>do not use it for commercial purposes; and</li>
        <li>do not distribute modified or derivative versions of it.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Fan art, translations, adaptations and other derivative work are genuinely welcome — but they
        fall outside this licence, so please write to
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> first. Permission is usually a formality.
      </p>

      <h2>Site code</h2>
      <p>
        The source code of this website — templates, styles and scripts, but not the story content or
        artwork — is licensed under the MIT Licence and is available in the
        <a href="https://github.com/Varnasr/theverylastsuperhero" rel="noopener">public repository</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Contributions to the Memory Wall</h2>
      <p>
        If you submit artwork or testimony, you confirm that it is your own work and that you have the
        right to share it. You keep ownership of it. You grant us a non-exclusive licence to display
        and archive it on this site with attribution, which you can withdraw at any time by writing to
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Submissions are reviewed by a person before anything appears. We may decline a contribution
        without giving a reason.
      </p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The site is provided as it is, without warranty of any kind. Availability is not guaranteed —
        it is a book's companion site, not infrastructure.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal { max-width: 46rem; }
  .page-head { margin-block-end: var(--space-l); }
  .lede { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--text-muted); }
  .legal h2 { font-size: var(--step-2); margin-block-start: var(--space-xl); }
  .legal ul { padding-inline-start: var(--space-m); color: var(--text-muted); }
</style>
